    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty strong take. You said a fully enforced border isn't even a matter of debate, but some economists argue that the influx of labor actually bolsters economic stability by filling critical gaps in the workforce and driving growth. How do you reconcile your stance with those economic arguments?",
